records.DESCRIPTION:
ABS Outstanding : SCR (Selective Catalytic Reduction) NOx Sensor was reported malfunction and in progress remotely troubleshoot with markers may spare part if require.
Master of this subject vessel confirmed that risk assessment was carried out with risk control measures was implemented onboard. All affected crew were informed regards to this failure. All other process parameters such as quenching temperature, including WMS, etc. had been stably maintained within the expected process range.
The owner's representative informed that the repair process had been continue troubleshooting with maker and lead time to resolve then require sufficient time.
In this regard, this Statutory Condition with a Conditional of International Air Pollution Prevention Certificate was issued valid up to two (2) month, 14 September 2026 pending the repair or replacement of SCR NOx Sensor as per Panama authorization letter No.111-01-004-DGMM-DOR/OPR, subject to the following conditions;
a. Risk assessment to be carried out with risk control measures to be implemented onboard;
b. All engineers and engine management team are to be made aware of the present inoperable condition of the main and/or auxiliary engine NOx Tier III;
c. The malfunction of Nox Sensor shall be recorded in the ship’s logbook; and
d. The Master shall report the defect to the competent coastal and port State authorities before entering the NOx Emission Control Area designated under MARPOL Annex VI and comply with any conditions that may be imposed by the coastal/port State authorities.
Remote survey was carried out review documents/photos as following:
1. Master and CE Attestation letter;
2. Risk assessment;
3. Bunker Delivery Note (BDN)
4. Engine Logbook & Fuel Changeover Record Book.
5. Photos shown NOx Sensor malfunction.
Upon satisfactory completion reviewed of the above, this Statutory Condition with a Conditional of International Air Pollution Prevention Certificate was issued valid up to two (2) month, 14 September 2026.
